cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Measuring Before Engraving: A Protocol for Curved Metal Surfaces"
message: "If you use this protocol or its results, please cite it. Keep the 'unverified' note until the results tables contain measurements."
type: dataset
version: "0.1"
date-released: "2026-10-04"
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  A measurement protocol for engraving and carving shallowly curved metal parts
  on flat-field two-axis galvo lasers and three-axis routers. Three claims,
  none yet measured: surface tilt is negligible below a sag-to-width ratio of
  about 4 per cent while defocus dominates; the Z correction a rotary fixture
  must apply is bounded by, and equal to, the part's own sag; and two
  measurements - sag in X and Y, against an empirically measured depth of field
  - are sufficient to select a correction method. Includes the measurement
  procedure, blank results tables, and a named falsification test for each
  claim.
keywords:
  - laser marking
  - galvo
  - fiber laser
  - depth of field
  - CNC
  - height mapping
  - curved surface engraving
  - measurement protocol
authors:
  - family-names: Gillie
    given-names: Lee
repository-code: "https://github.com/LeeGillie/curved-engraving-protocol"
notes: >-
  Developed in conversation with Claude (Anthropic, Opus 5). The optical
  calculations, geometric derivations and decision framework were worked out
  jointly; the questions, machines, parts and practical judgement are the
  author's. An AI system is not listed as an author because authorship carries
  accountability it cannot hold. See the Collaboration section of PROTOCOL.md
  for the full contribution statement.
